  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_astesi",
      "name": {
        "en": "Astesia's Badge",
        "zh": "星极证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_astesi",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Astesia has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for inflicting Arts damage on the enemy in close-quarters combat.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Guard Operator during field operations to exercise Arts Fighter responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员星极擅长在近身搏斗中对敌人造成法术杀伤\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为近卫干员，行使术战者职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_astesi",
      "name": {
        "en": "Unpredictable Star Chart",
        "zh": "未卜星图",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_astesi",
      "description": {
        "en": "'According to the most recent 'Startide freeze' calculations, these two stars have changed phases. But you still believe disaster is headed our way. Why is that?'\n'Hey, where'd you even come from, girlie? How am I supposed to sell these bracelets if I don't say that? Are you interested in astrology too? You seem like you come from a well-to-do family... Why don't I help you read the stars?'\n'Astrology is a complicated subject with a long history. Father said I wouldn't be able to understand the sky's appearance if I couldn't comprehend the ancient records, let alone read it.'\n'Hahaha. Don't break your brain with all that studying, my young friend.\n'Why don't you tell me, what's the point of reading the stars if not to give people empty comfort?'\n......\n'I'd like to resolve all your doubts in my father's stead, dear reporters.'\nFrancois Urbica is surrounded by reporters. They had failed to secure the rights to interview Rhine Lab personnel, so now they turn their resentment into ridicule towards the Astrological Research Association. A quiet Liberi girl walks up to them, and Francois raises an eyebrow, but does not stop her.\n'Astrology embodies humanity's earliest interest in the sky. When the first astrology study was published, aircraft had yet to leap into our skies, and Columbia wasn't even born yet. Scholars across generations have observed the starry sky day after day, and after every Startide, they would gather and process the complex data they received, overturning conclusions. There was only one thing keeping them going: the belief that our lives were entwined with the distant stars.\n'With today's technology, we can identify many errors in their past writings, but be it from the perspective of an astrologist or a historian, their meticulous records are still an incredible achievement. Perhaps we now believe that such ancient theories should be put to rest, but the hole above Trimounts is not the truth itself—it is a door we can all peek into. As a bibliography consultant for Rhine Lab, I know well that, be it through shared experience or objective inference, Casters of astrology and scholars of astronomy have always shared the same goal. It would be unfortunate to abandon our predecessors' research. If astrology says we can never truly understand the stars, then as a scholar, I will continue our search through the scientific method. But if there comes a day when science also fails to grasp the secrets that lie outside the dome, astrology may yet offer us a new possibility.'\n......\n'Is there something on my face, Elena?'\n'Do you still remember, Sia? When we were kids, you met a famous peddler who used astrology to swindle people. He made you so mad you cried all the way home. No one could get you to stop.'\n'*sigh* Are you here to laugh at me, then?'\n'No! I just meant, if it were the you from today, you'd have been able to shut that scammer up. Just like you shut up all those reporters earlier. I used to be a bit worried you'd be stuck under Father's influence if you kept studying the stars, but now I know I have nothing to worry about—\n'You were so cool just now, Sia!'",
        "zh": "“根据最近一次‘涌冻时刻’推算，这两颗星星形成的相位已经发生变化。您却依旧认为灾祸将至，这是为什么呢？”\n“嘿，哪来的小姑娘，不说这些我怎么把手串卖出去啊。你也对占星术感兴趣？看着像是大户人家的孩子……叔叔也帮你算算吧？”\n“占星是一门历史悠久的学问，父亲说如果不参透典籍就无法理解天空的样貌，更别提预言。”\n“哈哈哈小朋友，别把脑子学坏了。\n“你倒是告诉我，除了给人虚无的安慰之外，占星还有什么用处？”\n……\n“记者先生，我想替父亲解答你们的疑惑。”\n几名报刊记者围住了佛朗索瓦·乌比卡，他们并没有争取到采访莱茵生命相关人员的资格，此刻正把心中的怨气化作对占星研究协会的奚落。一名文静的黎博利女孩走到他们面前，佛朗索瓦挑了挑眉，并未阻止。\n“占星奇术承载着人类最早的对天空的好奇心。占星术师发表第一篇星象论文时，飞行器还未跃入空中，哥伦比亚也尚未建立。历代学者日复一日观测星空，每次‘星涌’过后又会处理庞杂的数据，推翻先前的结论，而支撑他们的只有一点——他们相信遥远的星辰与我们息息相关。\n“以现在的技术验算，当时的著作存在诸多谬误，然而无论是从星象学还是史学视角来看，那些记载仍有可取之处。或许在各位心中，古老的学说已被判处死刑。但特里蒙的空洞并非真相本身，而是一扇人人都能窥探的门扉。作为莱茵生命的文献学顾问，我深知无论是经验之谈还是客观推论，占星术师与天文学家的目标始终一致。舍弃前人的研究固然可惜，若占星学说无力对星象做出更多解释，作为一名学者，我将使用科研手段继续探索。但若有朝一日科学也无力把握苍穹之外的奥秘，占星学或许还能提供新的可能。”\n……\n“我的脸上有什么东西吗，埃琳娜。”\n“姐姐还记不记得，小时候你在路边遇到了一个借占星术的名头坑蒙拐骗的小贩，你被他气得不轻，回家之后还直掉眼泪，谁都哄不好。”\n“唉，你想笑就笑吧。”\n“我不是这个意思！现在的姐姐一定能把那个骗子说得哑口无言，那群来势汹汹的记者都不吱声了。本来我还担心，要是继续跟着父亲研究占星术你会摆脱不了他的影响，现在彻底放心啦——\n“刚才的姐姐非常帅气！”",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
